# OGRE — the chainsaw brute. A big, stooped hunk of primordial flesh lugging a
# chainsaw, in the lineage of Quake 1's Ogre: a bald bullet head sunk between
# a yoke of shoulder meat, a slab torso over a hanging gut, thick bowed legs,
# and forearms like hams. He does not stand up straight, ever.
#
# AUTHORED FROM PROSE. There is no reference mesh and no plate — the owner's
# brief was text ("a big brutish hunk of primordial flesh hunched over lugging
# a big chainsaw"), so blob:measure / blob:rings do not apply (exit 2 with no
# reference), and NO number below is measured against a mesh. Every number is
# a design decision and its comment says why. Cyberdemon.blob is the precedent
# for a prose-authored brute and the rig here borrows its leg proportions.
#
# THE SPLIT (owner's rule, 2026-09-08): the naked body is SDF — this file. The
# leather tunic, belt, strap, trousers and boots are MESH in ogre-kit.wam; the
# chainsaw is a HELD PROP (public/assets/lab/ogre-chainsaw.glb, generated by
# scripts/make-ogre-chainsaw.py in Blender) posed by the soldier's carry
# machinery, so both hands are on the saw by construction (carry.ts: right
# arm authored, left hand FABRIK'd onto the fore-grip).
#
# THE THREE BEATS that carry the silhouette:
#   1. THE HUNCH. Spine and chest pitch hard forward (world 20 and 28
#      degrees): a low, ape-like carriage, the yoke well ahead of the hips and
#      the head hung out in front on a short bull neck, brow first.
#   2. THE YOKE. A trapezius mass wider than the pelvis rides over the top of
#      the chest, so from the front the head is set INTO the shoulders, not on
#      top of them. A brute's head is small on a brute's body; that ratio is
#      the read (cyberdemon lesson).
#   3. THE ARMS. Upper arms and forearms thicker than the zombie's thighs, fists
#      the size of the head's jaw. Arms hang ahead of the body because the
#      body is hunched, which is where the chainsaw carry wants them anyway.
model ogre
  # Crown height. Standing upright he would be ~2.5 m; the hunch spends ~0.3 m
  # of it. 2.20 puts his brow over the soldier's (1.99) and the cyberdemon's
  # (2.15) crown, which is the "their heads tower over the other minions" read.
  height 2.20
  # Knees fold FORWARD. Checked, not decorative (blob-checks.ts checkStance).
  stance humanoid

skeleton
  # Hip line 1.12 (root 1.02 + len 0.10; children attach at the TAIL). That is
  # 0.51 of crown height — SHORT legs under a long, heavy torso is the brute
  # proportion. The pelvis len is the crotch-to-hip segment the WAM kit
  # needs as its `hips` bone.
  root pelvis at 1.02 len=0.10

  # THE HUNCH. dir angles are WORLD directions (blob-compile dirVector), not
  # relative to the parent, so these read directly: lumbar 20 degrees forward,
  # thoracic 28, carrying the chest top ~0.29 m ahead of the hips — a LOW,
  # ape-like hunch, and that is the character: owner, 2026-09-22, "i dont
  # mind the low gorilla hunch stance in fact i like that". (A 14/18 stoop
  # was tried the same day and reverted.)
  bone spine parent=pelvis dir=up pitch=20 len=0.36
  bone chest parent=spine  dir=up pitch=28 len=0.36
  # The neck leaves the yoke FORWARD (32 degrees) and the skull tips back 8,
  # so the face looks at the horizon out in front of the hunch. 40/0.12 sank
  # the face BELOW the yoke's crest (shoulders humped over the eyes); 32/0.14
  # lifts the jaw clear, and with the yoke kept FLAT (below) the face reads
  # from the front even in the hunch.
  bone neck  parent=chest  dir=up pitch=32 len=0.14
  bone skull parent=neck   dir=up pitch=-8 len=0.24

  mirror
    # Clavicles tilt UP 10 degrees: the shoulders are hunched high around the
    # neck, which is half of what sinks the head. 0.25 m of reach puts the
    # shoulder joint well outside the ribcage's 0.28 half-width, so the arm
    # starts in flesh (fused) and leaves it (daylight) — the goblin lesson is
    # that shoulder reach is a function of torso width, not a constant.
    bone clavicle parent=chest    dir=side tilt=10 len=0.27
    # Upper arms hang slightly forward and out around the gut. LONG ape arms
    # (0.46 + 0.46 m, fists near the knees): owner, 2026-09-22, "this
    # character should in some ways knuckle drag". It is also what lets the
    # dragged saw's nose reach the floor from a fist with a bent elbow — at
    # 0.83 m the arm had to lock straight and the hand lagged the grip.
    bone upperArm parent=clavicle dir=down pitch=12 tilt=20 len=0.46
    # Forearms reach FORWARD at rest (pitch 30): the hands hang in front of
    # the belly, the pose of something that carries a heavy tool all day. The
    # chainsaw carry rotates from here, so a forward rest also keeps the
    # carry's rotations small.
    bone foreArm  parent=upperArm dir=down pitch=30 tilt=2  len=0.46
    bone hand     parent=foreArm  dir=down pitch=20         len=0.15
    # Bowed legs: thighs splay out (tilt 7) and forward (pitch 14) around the
    # gut, shins come back in (tilt -6) and back (pitch -8) so the ankles land
    # under the knees' inside edge. Wide stance side=0.17 — the pelvis is
    # 0.54 m across, and the legs carry a body that is wider than it is deep.
    bone thigh    parent=pelvis dir=down pitch=14 tilt=7  side=0.17 len=0.53
    bone shin     parent=thigh  dir=down pitch=-8 tilt=-6          len=0.48
    bone foot     parent=shin   dir=fwd                            len=0.22
  end

body
  # ---- TORSO ---------------------------------------------------------------
  # Pelvis: broad and deep. The widest thing below the shoulders except the
  # gut — an ogre's hips are a barrel, not a waist.
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.40 r=0.205 wide=1.32 tall=0.95 deep=0.82 blend=0.040 offset=(0,0,0.060)
  # THE GUT. Hangs low and forward off the lumbar spine — the offset drops it
  # 5 cm and pushes it 9 cm ahead of the spine line so in profile it sags OVER
  # the belt (the kit's belt rides its underside). deep 1.12: it is round, not
  # a slab like the chest.
  blob torso on spine  at=0.25 r=0.215 wide=1.18 tall=1.05 deep=1.08 blend=0.070 offset=(0,-0.050,0.060)
  # Ribcage: barrel-chested, wider than deep.
  blob torso on spine  at=0.85 r=0.215 wide=1.28 tall=1.00 deep=1.00 blend=0.045
  # Upper chest slab — the widest torso mass, carrying the shoulders.
  blob torso on chest  at=0.50 r=0.220 wide=1.38 tall=1.00 deep=0.92 blend=0.045
  # Pectorals: two heavy slabs, sagging slightly (the offset drops them) —
  # old muscle gone to fat, not a bodybuilder's plates.
  blob torso on chest  at=0.45 r=0.110 wide=1.25 tall=0.85 deep=0.70 blend=0.014 offset=(0.105,-0.030,0.150) both
  # THE YOKE. A trapezius shelf wider than the pelvis, riding the top and BACK
  # of the chest (z offset -0.05 in world). FLAT (tall 0.62) and not raised:
  # the first pass (tall 0.80, lifted 4.5 cm, wide 1.85) humped above the
  # face and was half of the gorilla read. This mass is what the neck comes
  # out of.
  blob torso on chest  at=1.00 r=0.175 wide=1.70 tall=0.62 deep=1.00 blend=0.040 offset=(0,0.000,-0.050)
  # Upper-back mass behind the yoke — thick, but kept below the neck line
  # (r 0.170 lifted 3 cm was a silverback's hump).
  blob torso on chest  at=0.70 r=0.150 wide=1.30 tall=0.95 deep=0.90 blend=0.040 offset=(0,0.000,-0.080)

  # ---- HEAD ----------------------------------------------------------------
  # Bull neck: as wide as the head. deep 0.95 so it is not a pipe.
  bar head on neck from=0.00 to=1.00 r=0.105 deep=0.95 blend=0.012
  # CRANIUM — the "bullet-shaped hairless head". Taller than wide, and the
  # fattest unpainted head prim, so it is the decal's hs frame (the mouth
  # decal projects from it; cyberdemon lesson — pick the frame on purpose).
  blob head on skull at=0.60 r=0.120 wide=0.92 tall=1.28 deep=1.08 blend=0.008
  # JAW — wider than the cranium and slung low and forward: an underbite. The
  # width is what makes the head read as a brute from the front at distance;
  # the 5.5 cm jut is what reads in profile.
  blob head on skull at=0.22 r=0.095 wide=1.38 tall=0.82 deep=1.05 blend=0.008 offset=(0,-0.020,0.055)
  # Chin shelf under the underbite.
  blob head on skull at=0.10 r=0.055 wide=1.60 tall=0.70 deep=0.95 blend=0.006 offset=(0,-0.030,0.100)
  # BROW SHELF — one continuous bar, not two brows; chamfer keeps its lower
  # edge a crease the eyes can hide under. Reaches 0.157 m forward of the
  # skull axis against the cranium's 0.130 semi-depth: 2.7 cm proud.
  bar  head on skull from=0.62 to=0.62 r=0.036 wide=1.00 tall=0.80 blend=0.005 chamfer offset=(-0.080,0.000,0.108) tip=(0.160,0,0) bend=(0,0.008,0.030)
  # NOSE — a long, pointed, goblin-style spike (owner's pick 2026-09-22, over
  # the first pass's flat pug nose): the goblin's tapered, chamfered cone
  # scaled to the ogre and run nearly HORIZONTAL. Root inside the face at
  # z 0.115 (the cranium's semi-depth is 0.130), tip 0.16 m further out and
  # only 2 cm lower. The first hooked try dropped the tip onto the mouth and
  # clipped the lips; reach is the whole game (reference.md), so it goes OUT.
  blob head on skull at=0.47 r=0.030 r2=0.003 wide=0.85 blend=0.0030 chamfer offset=(0,0.004,0.115) tip=(0,-0.020,0.160) bend=(0,0.012,0.030)
  # Cheek slabs — the face is wider at the cheekbones than the cranium, which
  # makes the skull read as BULLET (narrow crown, broad face) not as egg.
  blob head on skull at=0.40 r=0.060 wide=1.00 tall=0.90 deep=0.90 blend=0.008 offset=(0.068,-0.005,0.060) both
  # Small, low, backswept pointed ears. r2 tapers to a point; tip sends it
  # back and slightly up, so it reads as a notch in the head's outline from
  # the front and a spike from the side.
  blob head on skull at=0.48 r=0.026 r2=0.004 wide=0.55 blend=0.004 chamfer offset=(0.104,0.000,-0.005) tip=(0.030,0.036,-0.048) both
  # LIPS — thick, meaty, PARTED (owner, 2026-09-22: "needs bigger thicker
  # lips"). No new primitive needed: each lip is one BENT bar across the
  # mouth, the same curved-capsule the brow shelf and the goblin's lips use.
  # The chord runs corner to corner and `bend=` bows the middle forward over
  # the jaw's curve and UP (upper) / the corners down (lower) — a grimace.
  # Measured off the face field at x 0 / x 0.075: surface z 0.378 / 0.342 at
  # the upper lip's height, 0.380 / 0.360 at the lower's, so each centreline
  # rides ~5 mm proud of the face. The gap between them (upper underside
  # y 1.968, lower top 1.956) is where the decal's cavity and teeth show, and
  # the decal's dark lip band lands ON these, tinting them. The lower lip is
  # fatter and further out: the underbite.
  #
  # UNPAINTED ON PURPOSE. With color= the renderer painted only the two END
  # caps (four dark balls at the mouth corners) while the CPU field and the
  # unpainted render both have the full curved lip: the per-prim paint pick
  # does not follow a large bend (a 3.6 cm bow on a 1.6 cm radius here). A
  # renderer bug, not the .blob's; flesh lips are right for an ogre anyway.
  bar  head on skull from=0.30 to=0.30 r=0.016 tall=0.95 blend=0.004 offset=(-0.075,-0.002,0.121) tip=(0.150,0,0) bend=(0,0.016,0.072)
  bar  head on skull from=0.30 to=0.30 r=0.020 tall=0.90 blend=0.004 offset=(-0.072,-0.048,0.136) tip=(0.144,0,0) bend=(0,0.012,0.052)
  # TUSKS — two lower canines jutting UP out of the underbite, past the upper
  # lip (z 0.149 so they rise in front of the geometric upper lip, not
  # through it). Ivory, not bone-white (the sheet multiplies albedo; pure white also
  # reads as plastic). Sharp: r2=0 is a true point.
  blob head on skull at=0.20 r=0.013 r2=0.000 blend=0.002 chamfer offset=(0.042,-0.004,0.149) tip=(0.006,0.052,0.010) bend=(0.004,0,0.010) both color=cdbf98 gloss=0.35
  # EYES — small, beady and sunk under the brow, GLOWING RED (owner,
  # 2026-09-22; the first pass was a dim sick yellow at glow 0.35). Emissive
  # prims, the gargoyle road (face.ts: geometric sockets never read). A hot
  # red at 0.9 is what reads from across a dark room — the eyes are the one
  # lit thing on him, under the brow shelf's shadow.
  blob head on skull at=0.58 r=0.014 blend=0.002 offset=(0.040,-0.006,0.118) both color=ff1a0a gloss=0.8 glow=0.9

  # ---- ARMS ----------------------------------------------------------------
  # Shoulder ball — deltoid and cap, the arm's structural mass (core).
  blob arm on upperArm at=0.05 r=0.150 blend=0.022 mirror core
  # Upper arm tapering to the elbow, then a bicep belly in front.
  bar  arm on upperArm from=0.10 to=0.92 r=0.130 r2=0.100 blend=0.018 mirror
  blob arm on upperArm at=0.45 r=0.100 wide=1.00 deep=1.10 blend=0.018 offset=(0,0,0.035) mirror
  # Forearm: FATTER at the elbow than the upper arm's end — the ham forearm is
  # the ogre arm's read. Tapers hard to the wrist.
  bar  arm on foreArm  from=0.02 to=0.92 r=0.125 r2=0.082 blend=0.018 mirror
  # Fist: the size of the jaw. Deep > wide so it reads as a closed hand.
  blob arm on hand at=0.50 r=0.098 wide=1.00 tall=1.10 deep=1.15 blend=0.016 mirror

  # ---- LEGS ----------------------------------------------------------------
  # Thigh root mass (core), then a thick tapered thigh. Most of this is under
  # the kit's trousers; it has to be right in SILHOUETTE because the trousers
  # are sized off it.
  blob leg on thigh at=0.05 r=0.180 blend=0.024 mirror core
  bar  leg on thigh from=0.10 to=0.94 r=0.172 r2=0.128 blend=0.020 mirror
  # Shin with a calf mass behind.
  bar  leg on shin  from=0.04 to=1.00 r=0.125 r2=0.085 blend=0.018 mirror
  blob leg on shin  at=0.28 r=0.112 wide=1.00 tall=1.20 deep=0.90 blend=0.018 offset=(0,-0.010,-0.045) mirror
  # Foot: broad and flat. The offset drops it onto the floor (ankle is at
  # y ~0.13); the boot in the kit covers it.
  blob leg on foot at=0.40 r=0.085 wide=1.25 tall=0.85 deep=2.30 blend=0.012 offset=(0,-0.070,0) mirror

# Wound pass: hidden bone. Auto-derive (ratio 0.38) handles the limbs; the
# skull is authored because a headshot is the shot players take.
bones
  ratio 0.38
  # Cranium bone: inside the flesh cranium (semi 0.110 x 0.154 x 0.130) with
  # ~2 cm of meat on every side.
  blob head on skull at=0.60 r=0.092 wide=0.95 tall=1.30 deep=1.05
  # Jaw bone, dropped onto the flesh jaw's centre.
  blob head on skull at=0.22 offset=(0,-0.025,0.050) r=0.075 wide=1.35 tall=0.75 deep=1.00

# THE FACE ROAD (cyberdemon/gargoyle precedent). No mesh, so no bake: all
# structure is prims above and the face block is a NUB — headRadius ~0 turns
# off the parameterised ellipsoid so it cannot fight the authored cranium.
face
  headRadius 0.001
  headWidth  1.0
  headHeight 1.0
  headDepth  1.0
  jawWidth   1.0
  jawHeight  1.0
  jawDrop    0
  jawJut     0
  noseLength 0
  noseWidth  1.0
  noseDrop   0
  browHeavy  0
  browRise   0
  headBlend  0.008

# A generated MOUTH decal at MULTIPLY (scripts/make-ogre-face.py): a wide,
# ragged grimace with a row of snaggle teeth. Eyes are prims, so the sheet's
# own glow is gated off (eyeGlowCut 0.99 / eyeGlowAmp 0 — the
# all-white-sheet-glows-red trap).
#
# hs is relative to the cranium prim (centre skull t0.60, semi 0.110 x 0.154
# x 0.130; centre y 2.050 since the posture pass). The mouth sits BETWEEN the
# geometric lips, 8.8 cm below the cranium centre (y 1.962): hs.y = -0.088 /
# 0.154 = -0.571. uv.y = hs.y*scale + centre, with the drawing centred at
# uv 0.5 -> centre = 0.5 + 0.571*0.22 = 0.626.
# Scale 0.22, not the first 0.30: at 0.30 the mouth rendered as a thin row of
# specks between the tusks in the close-up (projScale is a FREQUENCY — lower
# is bigger).
sheet
  image       ogre-face.png
  decal       0
  projScaleX  0.22
  projScaleY  0.22
  projCentreX 0.50
  projCentreY 0.626
  eyeGlowCut  0.99
  eyeGlowAmp  0

# Skin: a pale, sickly, pinkish-tan — raw hide that has never seen the sun,
# mottled toward a grey-green bruise so it reads as ROTTING rather than as a
# healthy man painted large. Linear RGB; the sRGB encode lifts it.
palette
  baseColor     0.400 0.270 0.215
  deepColor     0.470 0.070 0.070
  charColor     0.080 0.065 0.055
  # Oily, not wet: a broad, dull highlight.
  specIntensity 0.40
  specRoughness 0.50
  fresnelBoost  0.30
  translucency  0.18
  wetness       0.25
  # Low on purpose: at 0.05 / 0.02 the grain read as FUR from a few metres
  # (owner, 2026-09-22: "kinda looks like a gorilla or bigfoot"). Hide, not hair.
  surfaceNoiseAmp    0.025
  silhouetteNoiseAmp 0.008
  # Large blotches (scale ~1.8: hand-span patches) toward a cold grey-green
  # that differs in HUE from the base, so it reads as bruising IN the skin.
  mottleAmp     0.42
  mottleScale   1.8
  mottleColor   0.170 0.175 0.120
